[Proved] For all nearest-neighbor quadratic qubit bonds,
\[
e_0-E_{\mathrm{LTI}}(n)\le M\!\left[1-\cos\frac{\pi}{n+1}\right].
\]
I also constructed an explicit weighted-bond XX telescoping certificate with \(K=\pi\).

[Proved] Ring saturation is false, including its symmetry-twisted version. XX with field \(b=1/2\) supplies exact counterexamples at \(n=3,4\).

[Numerical] Ran the 62-bond scan, including 30 random bonds. Larger interacting computations and the largest-level search remain unrun, with SLURM scripts prepared. The general interacting LTI lemma remains open.

